Initial no. of moles $=\mathrm{n}_{1}=\mathrm{n}_{2}=\frac{\mathrm{n}}{2}$
finally when temp of 1 vessel is $T \&$ another is $2 T\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{n}_{1}=\frac{\mathrm{PV}}{\mathrm{RT}} \\
\mathrm{n}_{2}=\frac{\mathrm{PV}}{\mathrm{R} 2 \mathrm{~T}} \Rightarrow \frac{\mathrm{n}_{1}}{\mathrm{n}_{2}}=\frac{2}{1} \\
\mathrm{n}_{1}+\mathrm{n}_{2}=\mathrm{n} \\
\mathrm{n}_{1}=\frac{2 \mathrm{n}}{3} ; \mathrm{n}_{2}=\frac{\mathrm{n}}{3}
\end{array}
mass of gas $\propto \mathrm{n}_{1}\therefore \frac{\mathrm{M}_{2}}{\mathrm{M}_{1}}=\frac{\frac{\mathrm{n}}{3}}{\frac{\mathrm{n}}{2}}=\frac{2}{3}

$\mathrm{PV}=\mathrm{N} \times \mathrm{K} \times \mathrm{T}$
where $\mathrm{K}$ is Boltzmann constant
$\begin{array}{l}
10^{5} \times 100=\mathrm{N} \times 1.38 \times 10^{-23} \times 273 \\
\mathrm{~N} \approx 3 \times 10^{27}
\end{array}$

$P=\frac{-P_{0}}{V_{0}} V+P_{0}\&P V=n R T$
\begin{array}{l}
P V=n R T \\
\therefore T=\frac{P_{0} V}{R}\left[1-\frac{V}{V_{0}}\right]
\end{array}

